.Dd October 15, 2026
.Dt DOTFILES-WORKMUX 7
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm dotfiles-workmux
.Nd personal Git, Graphite, worktree, and tmux workflow
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
documents how I use workmux to give each branch its own Git worktree and
tmux session.
Workmux owns worktrees and sessions.
Graphite owns branch and stack topology when Graphite mode is enabled.
.Sh MENU
Press
.Ic C-a w
in tmux to open the workflow menu.
The active menu depends on the
.Ic @workflow
tmux option.
.Ss Git mode
.Bl -tag -width "add w/branch"
.It Ic add
Create or open a worktree using a branch name.
.It Ic add w/branch
Choose an existing local branch and open it in a worktree.
.It Ic add w/prompt
Create a named branch and save a prompt for the agent.
.It Ic open
Open the tmux session for an existing worktree.
.It Ic remove
Remove a worktree, its tmux session, and its local branch.
.It Ic close
Close the tmux session but keep the worktree and branch.
.It Ic dashboard
Open the workmux dashboard.
.It Ic sidebar
Toggle the workmux status sidebar.
.El
.Ss Graphite mode
.Bl -tag -width "new from trunk"
.It Ic new from trunk
Create a Graphite branch on trunk, then give it a worktree and tmux session.
.It Ic stack on current
Create a Graphite branch on the current branch, then give it a worktree and
tmux session.
.It Ic review branch
Choose an existing local branch and open it in a worktree.
This does not fetch a pull request.
.It Ic open
Open the tmux session for an existing worktree.
.It Ic discard
Remove the worktree and tmux session, then delete the local Graphite branch
and metadata.
This does not close or delete the remote pull request.
.It Ic close
Close the tmux session but keep the worktree and branch.
.It Ic dashboard
Open the workmux dashboard.
.It Ic graphite log
Show the local Graphite stack.
.It Ic sidebar
Toggle the workmux status sidebar.
.El
.Sh REVIEWING A PULL REQUEST
For an ordinary pull request, let workmux fetch it and create the worktree:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
workmux add --pr 12345
.Ed
.Pp
This is the default review flow.
It works for pull requests that do not need local Graphite stack metadata.
.Pp
When the review is finished, remove its worktree and local branch:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
workmux remove BRANCH
.Ed
.Sh REVIEWING A GRAPHITE STACK
Fetch the pull request and its Graphite metadata without changing the branch
in the current worktree:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
gt get 12345 --no-checkout
.Ed
.Pp
Then open
.Ic C-a w ,
choose
.Ic review branch ,
and select the fetched branch.
.Pp
Use
.Fl Fl no-checkout
because workmux needs to check the branch out in its own worktree.
Running
.Ic gt get
without it switches the current worktree and can prevent workmux from opening
the branch elsewhere.
.Pp
To edit someone else's Graphite branch, fetch it unfrozen:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
gt get 12345 --no-checkout --unfrozen
.Ed
.Sh WORKTREE LIFECYCLE
.Bl -tag -width "Remove"
.It Open
Use
.Ic open
to return to an existing worktree and tmux session.
.It Close
Use
.Ic close
when the worktree should remain available but its tmux session is no longer
needed.
.It Remove
Use
.Ic remove
for ordinary Git branches that are no longer needed.
.It Discard
Use
.Ic discard
for local Graphite branches that are no longer needed.
It only changes local state.
.El
.Sh COMMANDS TO AVOID
Do not use
.Ic gh pr checkout
or plain
.Ic gt checkout
to start a review worktree.
Those commands switch the current worktree and bypass workmux session
management.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Sy git-worktree(1) ,
.Sy tmux(1)
